 The seat runs `/ticket-loop` in its own context. The orchestrator does not absorb the
 implementation plan, code diffs, or review output — only the one-line result.
+
+**Park the queue item while the seat works (RIG-127).** The orchestrator makes no queue change
+while it waits, and its pane shows an idle prompt. An unparked claimed row then reads
+`stalled-after-claim` after `queue.pickup_stall_threshold_minutes` (3 min), and the stuck-sweep
+raises a false finding. A parked row reads `parked` and the sweep skips it. Park right after
+the `rig send`:
+
+```bash
+rig queue block ${QITEM_ID} \
+  --on "external:seat-result:${TICKET_ID}-${PHASE}" \
+  --continuation "awaiting ${SEAT} result for ${TICKET_ID} (${PHASE})" \
+  --wake-after 60m
+```
+
+- `${PHASE}` is `implement`, `validate` or `review`. The `external:` gate needs a body after the
+  prefix. A bare `external:` is refused.
+- `--wake-after` is the longest you will wait for this dispatch. The wake is the one nudge for the
+  park; when it fires, run the lease check below and re-park if the seat still works.
+- Send first, park second. If the result already arrived, do not park: the row is still
+  `in-progress`, so consume the result.
+- When the `TICKET_LOOP_RESULT` (or `REVIEW_RESULT`, `GATE_RESULT`) arrives, unpark before
+  anything else: `rig queue update ${QITEM_ID} --state in-progress --note "result: ${PHASE} ${OUTCOME}"`.
+- Several seats at once: park once, and unpark only when the continuation has what it needs
+  (any result or all results). Name which in `--continuation`.
+- A parked row still gets `unconsumed-wait` findings if a wake notice goes unread. Read wake
+  notices.
 
